00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:14,740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

1
00:01:42,305 --> 00:01:43,545
Thank you, Officer Ran.

2
00:01:43,625 --> 00:01:46,065
Oh, what's with all these gifts?

3
00:01:46,145 --> 00:01:48,585
-You shouldn't have.
-Chinese New Year is almost here.

4
00:01:49,465 --> 00:01:50,665
Anyway, Officer Ran,

5
00:01:52,105 --> 00:01:53,305
about the person named Yao Xincheng

6
00:01:54,145 --> 00:01:55,385
you asked about,

7
00:01:56,265 --> 00:01:57,585
I really don't remember anything.

8
00:01:58,585 --> 00:02:00,905
I never heard Uncle or Mengmeng
mention that name either.

9
00:02:00,985 --> 00:02:02,665
Uncle and Mengmeng
have been gone for five years now.

10
00:02:03,585 --> 00:02:05,065
The police also announced that.

11
00:02:05,585 --> 00:02:07,385
Wasn't the killer already dead?

12
00:02:07,465 --> 00:02:10,625
How is this still not over?

13
00:02:17,385 --> 00:02:20,665
If the truth hasn't come out,
how can it be over?

14
00:02:21,945 --> 00:02:23,425
Even if I'm gone,

15
00:02:23,945 --> 00:02:26,225
other police officers
will keep investigating.

16
00:02:27,465 --> 00:02:28,385
Right.

17
00:02:29,305 --> 00:02:30,505
Please think carefully again.

18
00:02:31,705 --> 00:02:35,025
<i>What did Officer Ran say to you?</i>

19
00:02:35,105 --> 00:02:36,665
<i>What did he ask about?</i>

20
00:02:37,465 --> 00:02:38,705
I remember

21
00:02:39,425 --> 00:02:41,705
Officer Ran made a phone call here.

22
00:02:41,785 --> 00:02:43,625
He called someone

23
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:46,545
with a two-character name.
Something Qiang.

24
00:02:47,145 --> 00:02:48,025
Qiang?

25
00:02:49,585 --> 00:02:50,505
Ma Qiang…

26
00:02:51,025 --> 00:02:53,385
-Was it Ma Qiang?
-<i>Yes.</i>

27
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:54,825
<i>That's it. Ma Qiang.</i>

28
00:02:54,905 --> 00:02:56,985
Ma Qiang… One moment.

29
00:02:58,585 --> 00:02:59,545
Right away.

30
00:03:05,745 --> 00:03:07,385
Alright. You can send it now.

31
00:03:07,465 --> 00:03:09,905
<i>Officer Ran, other than 1997 and 2002,</i>

32
00:03:09,985 --> 00:03:12,305
-<i>do you want the rest too?</i>
-Yes.

33
00:03:12,385 --> 00:03:13,465
I have those two years.

34
00:03:13,545 --> 00:03:15,145
Please send me the resident lists

35
00:03:15,225 --> 00:03:16,945
-for all the other years.
-<i>Alright. Right away.</i>

36
00:03:31,585 --> 00:03:33,425
RESIDENT LIST

37
00:03:42,625 --> 00:03:43,945
POLICE INTELLIGENCE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM

38
00:03:47,865 --> 00:03:53,025
"YAO XINCHENG" SEARCH RESULTS

39
00:03:53,105 --> 00:03:57,225
DAD

40
00:03:59,585 --> 00:04:00,425
Dad,

41
00:04:00,505 --> 00:04:02,945
I've searched both the internal network
and the public internet.

42
00:04:03,705 --> 00:04:05,065
There are all kinds of Yao Xinchengs.

43
00:04:05,145 --> 00:04:05,825
"YAO XINCHENG" SEARCH RESULTS

44
00:04:05,905 --> 00:04:06,945
Either they're not in Weiyang

45
00:04:07,025 --> 00:04:09,505
or they don't match Mr. Lu's description.

46
00:04:10,505 --> 00:04:11,705
Any leads on your side?

47
00:04:12,545 --> 00:04:14,825
Xu Meng's family doesn't know this person.

48
00:04:15,345 --> 00:04:17,225
I also asked Su Yuzhi and Lili.

49
00:04:17,305 --> 00:04:19,025
<i>They don't know this name either.</i>

50
00:04:21,585 --> 00:04:24,025
Qian Dajun cut the power again!

51
00:04:24,545 --> 00:04:27,185
Tomorrow, I'll cut his life short!

52
00:04:27,265 --> 00:04:28,345
<i>Dad.</i>

53
00:04:29,385 --> 00:04:31,225
Is everything alright in Yuanlongli?

54
00:04:31,905 --> 00:04:33,305
<i>Is Qian Dajun starting something again?</i>

55
00:04:33,385 --> 00:04:35,305
He's long gone now.

56
00:04:35,825 --> 00:04:37,385
After smashing the windows last night,

57
00:04:37,465 --> 00:04:39,385
everyone's waiting to deal with him.

58
00:04:43,745 --> 00:04:46,225
Kiddo, go to work tomorrow.

59
00:04:46,305 --> 00:04:48,505
If I find any clues here,
I'll let you know.

60
00:04:49,345 --> 00:04:50,825
-Hello?
-Hello?

61
00:04:52,305 --> 00:04:53,385
Dad?

62
00:04:54,465 --> 00:04:55,825
NO SERVICE

63
00:04:55,905 --> 00:04:57,345
Jeez.

64
00:04:58,945 --> 00:05:00,185
Ma Qiang.

65
00:05:01,105 --> 00:05:01,945
Mr. He.

66
00:05:02,865 --> 00:05:05,065
I called you. Why didn't you answer?

67
00:05:05,665 --> 00:05:08,945
I'm sorry, Mr. He.
I was with Mr. Qian all night.

68
00:05:09,025 --> 00:05:11,145
I didn't dare answer. What do you need?

69
00:05:11,825 --> 00:05:14,225
The night before New Year's Eve in 2003,

70
00:05:14,305 --> 00:05:16,705
did Officer Ran call you?

71
00:05:17,425 --> 00:05:19,985
That was so long ago.
How could I remember?

72
00:05:21,545 --> 00:05:23,505
The day before Ran passed away.

73
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:31,305
Yes, I remember now. Officer Ran
called me then and asked

74
00:05:31,385 --> 00:05:32,745
for Yuanlongli's resident lists
from the past years.

75
00:05:33,345 --> 00:05:35,225
Later, he came
to the property office himself

76
00:05:35,305 --> 00:05:36,505
and even brought New Year gifts.

77
00:05:37,025 --> 00:05:37,945
YUANLONGLI PROPERTY MANAGEMENT

78
00:05:38,025 --> 00:05:40,305
Thank you, Officer Ran. You're too kind.

79
00:05:40,385 --> 00:05:41,465
You still remember us.

80
00:05:42,305 --> 00:05:43,465
Have a seat.

81
00:05:43,545 --> 00:05:44,665
Please sit.

82
00:05:46,185 --> 00:05:48,745
It's almost Chinese New Year.
You all work hard year-round.

83
00:05:49,705 --> 00:05:53,745
Our job can't compare to yours at all.

84
00:05:54,585 --> 00:05:55,785
By the way,

85
00:05:55,865 --> 00:05:58,625
do you remember
if there was someone in Yuanlongli

86
00:05:58,705 --> 00:06:00,025
named Yao Xincheng?

87
00:06:00,105 --> 00:06:00,865
Yao Xincheng?

88
00:06:02,265 --> 00:06:03,705
I really don't know.

89
00:06:04,305 --> 00:06:06,025
What about relatives of the residents?

90
00:06:06,625 --> 00:06:08,385
I know even less about that.

91
00:06:13,505 --> 00:06:14,385
Where's Mr. Qian?

92
00:06:14,465 --> 00:06:16,265
I called him several times,
but he didn't answer.

93
00:06:17,105 --> 00:06:19,305
Mr. Qian went out
this afternoon for business drinks.

94
00:06:19,385 --> 00:06:22,665
At this hour,
he's probably hammered already.

95
00:06:24,105 --> 00:06:25,225
Officer Ran,

96
00:06:25,305 --> 00:06:27,545
I'm about to head back
to my village for Chinese New Year.

97
00:06:27,625 --> 00:06:29,185
Wang Xinglong is on duty tomorrow.

98
00:06:29,265 --> 00:06:30,145
How about this?

99
00:06:30,665 --> 00:06:32,625
I'll leave a note for Mr. Qian.

100
00:06:32,705 --> 00:06:34,705
When he sees it, he'll call you back.

101
00:06:35,505 --> 00:06:36,425
Alright.

102
00:06:36,505 --> 00:06:37,905
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

103
00:06:40,465 --> 00:06:41,385
Officer Ran.

104
00:06:42,505 --> 00:06:45,905
You mentioned this Yao Xincheng.

105
00:06:45,985 --> 00:06:48,545
Does he have anything to do
with Yuanlongli?

106
00:06:56,145 --> 00:06:58,905
If he has nothing to do
with Yuanlongli either,

107
00:07:00,145 --> 00:07:02,665
then I don't know where I can go next.

108
00:07:07,425 --> 00:07:08,425
And then?

109
00:07:08,505 --> 00:07:09,625
And then…

110
00:07:10,625 --> 00:07:12,105
That was all.

111
00:07:12,625 --> 00:07:16,105
When Officer Ran left,
he looked pretty disappointed.

112
00:07:22,665 --> 00:07:23,785
I never thought

113
00:07:24,945 --> 00:07:28,425
that would be the last time I saw him.

114
00:08:14,905 --> 00:08:15,585
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

115
00:08:15,665 --> 00:08:16,505
<i>Say, sir,</i>

116
00:08:16,585 --> 00:08:18,785
<i>do you remember the blue leather heels</i>
<i>from the June 30th case?</i>

117
00:08:18,865 --> 00:08:21,305
<i>The blue leather heels</i>
<i>were tall and eye-catching.</i>

118
00:08:21,385 --> 00:08:22,345
<i>They were definitely real.</i>

119
00:08:22,425 --> 00:08:23,265
BLUE LEATHER HEELS
LILI

120
00:08:23,345 --> 00:08:24,185
DU MINGLIANG'S MOTHER

121
00:08:24,265 --> 00:08:26,825
<i>You should ask those who sell fake shoes.</i>

122
00:08:26,905 --> 00:08:28,505
<i>They would definitely know.</i>

123
00:08:28,585 --> 00:08:31,145
<i>Judging by the finish and workmanship,</i>

124
00:08:31,225 --> 00:08:33,825
<i>that should be the work</i>
<i>of Mr. Lu from Pingzhao County.</i>

125
00:08:34,425 --> 00:08:36,705
<i>It was a perfectly real pair of shoes,</i>
<i>yet he insisted I make them look fake.</i>

126
00:08:37,305 --> 00:08:38,745
<i>He was a man in his thirties.</i>

127
00:08:38,825 --> 00:08:39,784
SHOEMAKER MR. LU
MAN WITH THREE CIGARETTE BURN MARKS

128
00:08:39,865 --> 00:08:42,545
<i>He had three burn marks on his arm.</i>

129
00:08:43,865 --> 00:08:45,985
<i>There's a loose thread here.</i>

130
00:08:46,065 --> 00:08:47,065
<i>How did I never notice it before?</i>

131
00:08:47,145 --> 00:08:47,825
BOWLS DRESS

132
00:08:47,905 --> 00:08:49,425
<i>According to the dry-cleaning records,</i>

133
00:08:49,505 --> 00:08:53,145
<i>the buyer of this dress</i>
<i>was named Yao Xincheng.</i>

134
00:08:53,665 --> 00:08:56,345
<i>If he has nothing to do with Yuanlongli,</i>

135
00:08:56,425 --> 00:08:59,305
<i>then I don't know where I can go next.</i>

136
00:09:18,625 --> 00:09:19,665
Ran.

137
00:09:22,665 --> 00:09:25,345
How did you continue the investigation?

138
00:09:51,105 --> 00:09:52,105
Sir,

139
00:09:53,465 --> 00:09:54,865
if you were me,

140
00:09:55,905 --> 00:09:57,585
how would you continue the investigation?

141
00:11:37,825 --> 00:11:42,825
WEIYANG PUBLIC SECURITY BUREAU
NANSHAN BRANCH

142
00:11:42,905 --> 00:11:46,985
LOYAL AND TRUE

143
00:11:50,705 --> 00:11:51,665
Hello, Dad?

144
00:11:51,745 --> 00:11:53,225
What did you find?

145
00:11:53,305 --> 00:11:56,585
-I'm going home.
-What? Not investigating anymore?

146
00:11:56,665 --> 00:11:59,065
<i>I was thinking</i>
<i>I would come to your place after work.</i>

147
00:11:59,665 --> 00:12:01,025
The trail went cold.

148
00:12:01,625 --> 00:12:03,945
I don't want to stay stuck
in Yuanlongli anymore.

149
00:12:04,025 --> 00:12:05,065
I'll head home

150
00:12:05,665 --> 00:12:07,185
and think about the next move.

151
00:12:08,025 --> 00:12:08,985
Alright then.

152
00:12:09,065 --> 00:12:11,065
I'll help you move after work.

153
00:12:11,585 --> 00:12:14,065
No need. You take care of your work.

154
00:12:14,145 --> 00:12:16,825
I can handle these myself.

155
00:12:18,025 --> 00:12:19,265
Dad,

156
00:12:19,865 --> 00:12:20,905
are you alright?

157
00:12:22,745 --> 00:12:24,705
Why wouldn't I be?

158
00:12:26,905 --> 00:12:28,465
Just focus on your job.

159
00:12:28,545 --> 00:12:31,985
<i>If I find any new clues,</i>
<i>I'll tell you right away.</i>

160
00:12:33,065 --> 00:12:37,625
Don't worry. In my life,
there's no such word as giving up.

161
00:12:38,225 --> 00:12:39,145
I'm hanging up.

162
00:13:29,305 --> 00:13:30,225
Coming.

163
00:13:35,305 --> 00:13:36,265
Who is it?

164
00:13:39,345 --> 00:13:40,905
Officer He, morning.

165
00:13:41,905 --> 00:13:44,745
Manager Ma sent me over
to bring you hot water.

166
00:13:46,065 --> 00:13:47,225
There's no need.

167
00:13:47,305 --> 00:13:49,225
I'm moving out soon anyway.

168
00:13:51,465 --> 00:13:52,785
Are you moving out?

169
00:13:54,425 --> 00:13:55,345
That's great.

170
00:13:55,425 --> 00:13:56,945
I'll give you a hand.

171
00:13:57,025 --> 00:13:59,225
No need. You go get busy.

172
00:14:03,305 --> 00:14:05,305
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

173
00:14:08,265 --> 00:14:10,145
Poor Officer Ran.

174
00:14:12,745 --> 00:14:14,105
Speaking of that,

175
00:14:14,625 --> 00:14:17,625
before he passed, I saw him one last time.

176
00:14:22,545 --> 00:14:23,385
Then…

177
00:14:24,545 --> 00:14:25,625
What did you say?

178
00:14:28,985 --> 00:14:30,865
You saw him? When?

179
00:14:30,945 --> 00:14:32,905
On New Year's Eve morning.

180
00:14:33,625 --> 00:14:34,745
In this building.

181
00:14:44,785 --> 00:14:45,985
Who the heck is that?

182
00:14:47,505 --> 00:14:48,665
I'm sorry, Wang Xinglong.

183
00:14:49,265 --> 00:14:50,105
Officer Ran?

184
00:14:50,185 --> 00:14:51,345
It's alright.

185
00:14:51,425 --> 00:14:53,145
You really startled me.

186
00:14:54,185 --> 00:14:55,945
<i>When he came out of the elevator,</i>
<i>he scared me.</i>

187
00:14:56,465 --> 00:14:57,505
His eyes were bloodshot.

188
00:14:57,585 --> 00:14:58,945
He clearly didn't sleep all night.

189
00:14:59,025 --> 00:15:00,625
<i>Then he rushed off in a hurry.</i>

190
00:15:01,225 --> 00:15:03,705
Must've been heading off
to something urgent.

191
00:15:09,145 --> 00:15:11,305
Are you sure
it was New Year's Eve morning?

192
00:15:13,025 --> 00:15:15,105
I'm sure. Eight in the morning.

193
00:15:15,625 --> 00:15:16,825
It was a property management rule.

194
00:15:16,905 --> 00:15:19,265
Eight a.m. Patrol the building at 8 a.m.

195
00:15:20,985 --> 00:15:21,905
DRAFT, UNSENT MESSAGE

196
00:15:21,985 --> 00:15:23,345
SAVED TIME: 2003-01-31
13:09:37, RECIPIENT: SIR

197
00:15:23,425 --> 00:15:24,825
RAN: SIR, THE JUNE 30TH CASE IS WRONG
THE WHOLE THING IS WRONG

198
00:15:33,345 --> 00:15:34,225
Thank you.

199
00:15:34,305 --> 00:15:36,145
You did me a big favor.

200
00:15:38,785 --> 00:15:40,625
Wait, Mr. He… Weren't you moving out?

201
00:15:40,705 --> 00:15:41,545
Why are you moving things back in?

202
00:15:41,625 --> 00:15:44,065
I'm not moving anymore.
Absolutely not moving.

203
00:15:45,065 --> 00:15:48,025
By the way,
go find Qian Dajun now and tell him

204
00:15:48,705 --> 00:15:50,905
I'm staying in Yuanlongli,
and I'll fight him to the end.

205
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:54,185
That's a snap decision.

206
00:16:02,785 --> 00:16:05,585
Ran met with Ma Qiang

207
00:16:05,665 --> 00:16:07,705
the night before New Year's Eve.

208
00:16:09,545 --> 00:16:11,385
Then on New Year's Eve morning,

209
00:16:11,465 --> 00:16:13,305
he ran out of the building again.

210
00:16:15,025 --> 00:16:16,865
His eyes were red with exhaustion.

211
00:16:17,785 --> 00:16:21,145
That afternoon, he drafted a message to me

212
00:16:21,665 --> 00:16:24,185
saying the June 30th case was all wrong.

213
00:16:26,545 --> 00:16:28,425
He must have found something.

214
00:16:29,945 --> 00:16:32,385
He must have found something
in this building.

215
00:16:32,465 --> 00:16:33,305
<i>CRIMINAL CASE STUDIES</i>

216
00:16:36,225 --> 00:16:38,385
RAN FANGXU'S PATH

217
00:16:40,785 --> 00:16:41,825
Ran,

218
00:16:42,425 --> 00:16:44,345
what did you find?

219
00:17:21,985 --> 00:17:24,585
SIR

220
00:17:44,105 --> 00:17:47,985
<i>In four hours,</i>
<i>we'll welcome the Chinese New Year.</i>

221
00:17:48,065 --> 00:17:49,905
<i>On the last night</i>
<i>before the fresh new year,</i>

222
00:17:49,985 --> 00:17:54,025
<i>are you, listening to the radio,</i>
<i>on your way to reunite with your family?</i>

223
00:17:57,105 --> 00:18:00,865
BLESSING

224
00:18:22,145 --> 00:18:23,985
Why won't he answer?

225
00:18:26,985 --> 00:18:28,425
Dad, don't worry.

226
00:18:28,505 --> 00:18:30,865
Uncle Ran has probably gone
to pick up Ms. Qiao.

227
00:18:32,705 --> 00:18:34,305
See? Here they are.

228
00:18:35,265 --> 00:18:36,305
Coming.

229
00:18:39,825 --> 00:18:41,065
-Qiao.
-Officer He.

230
00:18:41,145 --> 00:18:42,185
Ms. Qiao.

231
00:18:42,265 --> 00:18:43,905
-Xiaohe.
-Come in.

232
00:18:43,985 --> 00:18:44,665
Sure.

233
00:18:45,585 --> 00:18:46,985
Ran didn't come with you?

234
00:18:48,865 --> 00:18:51,585
I thought something had come up
at work and kept him busy.

235
00:18:51,665 --> 00:18:54,305
He was supposed to pick me up from work.

236
00:18:54,385 --> 00:18:56,905
I waited, and he never showed.

237
00:18:56,985 --> 00:18:57,945
He didn't answer my calls either.

238
00:18:58,025 --> 00:18:59,505
I was worried
you would all be waiting too long,

239
00:18:59,585 --> 00:19:01,625
so I took a taxi here.

240
00:19:03,185 --> 00:19:04,425
That brat.

241
00:19:04,505 --> 00:19:06,425
What is he busy with on New Year's Eve?

242
00:19:06,505 --> 00:19:09,345
Maybe he left his phone back at work.

243
00:19:10,025 --> 00:19:12,465
It's raining hard outside today.
The roads are bad.

244
00:19:12,545 --> 00:19:13,785
Let's wait for him.

245
00:19:14,745 --> 00:19:16,305
Alright. Let's go inside.

246
00:19:17,625 --> 00:19:19,905
Officer He, I'm not good at picking gifts,

247
00:19:19,985 --> 00:19:21,545
so I brought some supplements.

248
00:19:22,345 --> 00:19:23,185
Just having you here is enough.

249
00:19:23,265 --> 00:19:24,865
You don't have to bring
anything next time.

250
00:19:24,945 --> 00:19:26,945
Xiaohe, help Ms. Qiao change clothes

251
00:19:27,025 --> 00:19:27,985
-and get her a pair of slippers.
-Okay.

252
00:19:28,065 --> 00:19:29,465
I'll finish wrapping dumplings.

253
00:19:29,545 --> 00:19:32,225
-Ms. Qiao, here.
-Thank you.

254
00:19:35,105 --> 00:19:36,425
Come. New Year's gift.

255
00:19:40,065 --> 00:19:42,265
We have the same scarf.
Thank you, Ms. Qiao.

256
00:19:42,345 --> 00:19:43,385
You're welcome.

257
00:19:45,705 --> 00:19:46,865
Have a seat.

258
00:19:46,945 --> 00:19:47,785
Sure.

259
00:19:49,425 --> 00:19:51,585
This scarf matches my hairstyle perfectly.

260
00:19:52,305 --> 00:19:55,225
By the way,
did Uncle Ran get you a gift too?

261
00:19:58,305 --> 00:19:59,385
Oh…

262
00:20:00,065 --> 00:20:01,865
Looks like the answer is obvious.

263
00:20:06,865 --> 00:20:07,945
Officer He, I'll help.

264
00:20:09,465 --> 00:20:10,825
Alright. Good to have extra hands.

265
00:20:16,065 --> 00:20:16,905
Qiao,

266
00:20:17,905 --> 00:20:20,585
my apprentice is good in every way.

267
00:20:21,185 --> 00:20:22,425
Stable job.

268
00:20:22,945 --> 00:20:24,545
Good character.

269
00:20:24,625 --> 00:20:26,105
Only one flaw.

270
00:20:26,745 --> 00:20:29,305
Other than solving cases,
he never takes the initiative in anything.

271
00:20:31,145 --> 00:20:35,185
You see, as his mentor,
when it comes to marriage,

272
00:20:35,265 --> 00:20:37,225
I can count as half a parent.

273
00:20:38,705 --> 00:20:39,745
Look,

274
00:20:39,825 --> 00:20:41,145
Xiaohe likes you so much.

275
00:20:42,145 --> 00:20:44,825
Our big family here
just happens to be missing one person.

276
00:20:44,905 --> 00:20:47,185
We genuinely hope
you'll become that person.

277
00:20:48,065 --> 00:20:49,385
That's right, Ms. Qiao.

278
00:20:49,465 --> 00:20:52,425
From the first time I met you,
I felt like you would become family.

279
00:20:53,025 --> 00:20:54,345
Once Uncle Ran gets here,

280
00:20:54,425 --> 00:20:56,745
I'm calling you Mrs. Ran.

281
00:20:58,825 --> 00:20:59,665
Qiao,

282
00:20:59,745 --> 00:21:01,705
no matter how things develop
between you and Ran later,

283
00:21:02,305 --> 00:21:04,745
fast or slow, that's between you two.

284
00:21:04,825 --> 00:21:05,745
I won't interfere.

285
00:21:05,825 --> 00:21:07,385
But one thing I'll say first.

286
00:21:07,465 --> 00:21:09,785
This home will be your home from now on.

287
00:21:10,705 --> 00:21:13,265
We gather like this
every holiday and festival.

288
00:21:42,265 --> 00:21:44,905
In a little while,
the New Year bell will ring.

289
00:21:45,505 --> 00:21:46,785
I should make a wish.

290
00:21:47,385 --> 00:21:49,065
I wish our whole family

291
00:21:49,585 --> 00:21:53,065
happiness and many blessings.

292
00:21:57,185 --> 00:21:58,225
Thank you,

293
00:21:58,745 --> 00:21:59,585
Officer He.

294
00:22:00,185 --> 00:22:01,625
Thank you, Xiaohe.

295
00:22:02,585 --> 00:22:04,945
And even more, I should thank Ran.

296
00:22:06,465 --> 00:22:07,705
Thank you all

297
00:22:08,865 --> 00:22:10,705
for making me feel
what having a family is like.

298
00:22:11,425 --> 00:22:12,865
That's my wish too.

299
00:22:14,585 --> 00:22:15,785
My New Year's wish.

300
00:22:18,785 --> 00:22:19,825
Why thank us?

301
00:22:20,345 --> 00:22:22,545
From now on, we're family.

302
00:22:22,625 --> 00:22:23,985
No need for thanks between family.

303
00:22:24,505 --> 00:22:25,625
Exactly.

304
00:22:25,705 --> 00:22:27,745
No worries there, Mrs. Ran.

305
00:22:28,785 --> 00:22:32,145
<i>I want love to live in my home every day</i>

306
00:22:32,225 --> 00:22:33,585
<i>Day and night</i>

307
00:22:33,665 --> 00:22:35,545
<i>Through all four seasons</i>

308
00:22:35,625 --> 00:22:37,145
<i>With our hearts</i>

309
00:22:37,225 --> 00:22:38,985
<i>Loving our home</i>

310
00:22:39,065 --> 00:22:42,385
<i>I want love to live in your home every day</i>

311
00:22:42,465 --> 00:22:45,705
<i>I want love to live in my home every day</i>

312
00:22:45,785 --> 00:22:47,345
<i>Filled with joy</i>

313
00:22:47,425 --> 00:22:49,625
<i>Safe and blessed</i>

314
00:22:49,705 --> 00:22:51,065
<i>Love stays in our home</i>

315
00:22:51,145 --> 00:22:51,825
RAN

316
00:22:51,905 --> 00:22:55,465
<i>Forever</i>

317
00:23:30,505 --> 00:23:34,745
SIR

318
00:24:04,505 --> 00:24:06,345
It's mainly because of the oil drums.

319
00:24:07,225 --> 00:24:08,985
Recheck the scene.

320
00:24:10,905 --> 00:24:13,425
Director Zou, this belongs to Captain Ran.

321
00:24:16,865 --> 00:24:18,185
It's burned in the fire.

322
00:24:19,905 --> 00:24:22,465
There are no cameras on this road.

323
00:24:23,225 --> 00:24:24,785
Based on our initial investigation,

324
00:24:25,305 --> 00:24:27,825
the accident was likely caused
by poorly stored materials

325
00:24:27,905 --> 00:24:29,665
at this construction site.

326
00:24:30,665 --> 00:24:32,665
Strong wind knocked over two fuel drums.

327
00:24:33,225 --> 00:24:34,385
It was raining hard and dark outside.

328
00:24:35,745 --> 00:24:37,185
Oil spilled onto the road,
making it slippery.

329
00:24:38,385 --> 00:24:41,505
When the vehicle passed through,
it would've been hard to keep control.

330
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:44,345
That's why Captain Ran…

331
00:24:46,625 --> 00:24:48,265
Coordinate with the criminal department.

332
00:24:48,865 --> 00:24:50,465
You must get to the bottom of this.

333
00:24:53,305 --> 00:24:55,025
He was a good coworker

334
00:24:55,105 --> 00:24:56,625
and a good comrade.

335
00:24:58,945 --> 00:25:00,265
It's heartbreaking.

336
00:25:10,185 --> 00:25:11,505
Uncle Ran!

337
00:25:12,105 --> 00:25:13,425
Uncle Ran!

338
00:25:13,505 --> 00:25:14,825
-Uncle Ran!
-Xiaohe.

339
00:25:15,625 --> 00:25:16,985
Don't go over there.

340
00:25:17,065 --> 00:25:20,665
Don't. Xiaohe, don't go over there.

341
00:29:00,665 --> 00:29:01,825
Ran.

342
00:29:05,065 --> 00:29:06,265
It's Chinese New Year.

343
00:29:18,785 --> 00:29:19,785
It's Chinese New Year.

344
00:29:32,185 --> 00:29:33,985
<i>Wishing everyone a Happy Chinese New Year!</i>

345
00:29:34,065 --> 00:29:35,785
-<i>Wish you a happy Year of the Goat!</i>
-<i>Happy New Year!</i>

346
00:29:35,865 --> 00:29:37,745
<i>Happy Chinese New Year!</i>

347
00:29:37,825 --> 00:29:40,545
<i>Dear friends, at this exciting moment,</i>

348
00:29:40,625 --> 00:29:42,545
<i>we send to people</i>
<i>of all ethnic groups across the nation,</i>

349
00:29:42,625 --> 00:29:44,225
<i>to our compatriots</i>

350
00:29:44,305 --> 00:29:45,265
<i>in Hong Kong, China,</i>
<i>Macau Special Administrative Region,</i>

351
00:29:45,345 --> 00:29:48,385
<i>Taiwan, China, and to Chinese people</i>
<i>all around the world</i>

352
00:29:48,465 --> 00:29:49,305
<i>our New Year greetings.</i>

353
00:29:49,385 --> 00:29:52,905
<i>Crossing the threshold of time,</i>
<i>we step into the embrace of spring.</i>

354
00:29:52,985 --> 00:29:55,065
<i>Happy Spring Festival!</i>

355
00:30:13,625 --> 00:30:18,265
RAN FANGXU, MALE, CREMATION IN PROGRESS

356
00:30:18,345 --> 00:30:21,865
IN PROGRESS

357
00:30:25,545 --> 00:30:27,705
IN MOURNING

358
00:30:50,345 --> 00:30:51,985
Xiaohe, where are you going?

359
00:31:11,065 --> 00:31:12,865
-I win.
-That's your…

360
00:31:12,945 --> 00:31:14,265
Someone's here.

361
00:31:14,345 --> 00:31:16,265
LANYA HAIR SALON

362
00:31:16,345 --> 00:31:18,425
FULL SALON SERVICES
CUTS, COLORS &amp; STYLES

363
00:31:18,505 --> 00:31:20,065
We're closed today.

364
00:31:22,145 --> 00:31:23,385
I need a haircut.

365
00:31:37,225 --> 00:31:38,065
<i>Xiaohe.</i>

366
00:31:38,705 --> 00:31:40,065
Say hi to Uncle Ran.

367
00:31:41,105 --> 00:31:42,545
Hello, Xiaohe.

368
00:31:47,265 --> 00:31:48,625
This is for you.

369
00:31:48,705 --> 00:31:50,025
<i>Thank you, Uncle Ran.</i>

370
00:31:58,385 --> 00:32:00,065
Let go of me. I'm not going with you.

371
00:32:00,145 --> 00:32:02,225
I even treated you as my best friend!

372
00:32:05,585 --> 00:32:07,825
Xiaohe, I owe you an apology.

373
00:32:07,905 --> 00:32:11,745
The way you acted in the traffickers' van
was brave and smart.

374
00:32:11,825 --> 00:32:13,385
You surely are cut out for a detective.

375
00:32:17,025 --> 00:32:18,745
From now on, you teach me music notation,

376
00:32:18,825 --> 00:32:20,065
I teach you criminal investigation.

377
00:32:20,145 --> 00:32:21,145
We'll learn from each other.

378
00:32:21,745 --> 00:32:23,985
-Deal.
-Deal.

379
00:32:44,145 --> 00:32:46,265
RAN 1972-2003

380
00:33:02,785 --> 00:33:07,865
TOMB OF RAN FANGXU

381
00:33:07,945 --> 00:33:08,985
First bow.

382
00:33:13,625 --> 00:33:14,465
Second bow.

383
00:33:25,025 --> 00:33:25,945
Third bow.

384
00:33:41,545 --> 00:33:42,625
Uncle Ran.

385
00:36:25,865 --> 00:36:27,145
Hello. My surname is Ran.

386
00:36:27,225 --> 00:36:29,385
-Ran as in rising upward.
-This is my apprentice.

387
00:36:29,465 --> 00:36:30,585
I'm not.

388
00:36:31,705 --> 00:36:32,385
He's not my mentor.

389
00:36:33,385 --> 00:36:34,665
Let me say this again.

390
00:36:34,745 --> 00:36:35,785
I am not your apprentice.

391
00:36:38,785 --> 00:36:39,705
He Yuanhang!

392
00:36:39,785 --> 00:36:41,105
I got him! He Yuanhang.

393
00:36:41,185 --> 00:36:42,945
He Yuanhang,
you're not fit to be a detective!

394
00:36:43,025 --> 00:36:43,985
MISSING PERSON

395
00:36:51,905 --> 00:36:54,905
I'll follow your lead.
Let's do the plan you talked about.

396
00:36:54,985 --> 00:36:57,465
This time, you're the one who begged me.

397
00:36:58,145 --> 00:36:59,225
Aren't we partners?

398
00:37:00,625 --> 00:37:02,945
Look at you.
You work pretty well together.

399
00:37:16,425 --> 00:37:17,625
He!

400
00:37:18,465 --> 00:37:19,585
He!

401
00:37:21,345 --> 00:37:22,225
He!

402
00:37:22,745 --> 00:37:24,505
Don't sleep, He.

403
00:37:24,585 --> 00:37:26,225
Comrade He Yuanhang, you're hereby awarded

404
00:37:26,305 --> 00:37:27,745
Second-class Merit for Individual Service.

405
00:37:40,865 --> 00:37:42,065
I'm leaving,

406
00:37:43,025 --> 00:37:43,985
sir.

407
00:37:53,705 --> 00:37:54,625
Kiddo.

408
00:37:56,185 --> 00:37:57,705
I only ask one thing of you.

409
00:37:58,705 --> 00:37:59,705
Dad,

410
00:38:00,425 --> 00:38:01,345
say no more.

411
00:38:02,265 --> 00:38:05,305
After the holiday,
I'll go back to school and study.

412
00:38:05,905 --> 00:38:06,825
I'll apply to the police academy

413
00:38:07,705 --> 00:38:08,945
and become a detective.

414
00:38:09,545 --> 00:38:10,625
I'll solve cases

415
00:38:11,705 --> 00:38:13,105
and finish the shifts

416
00:38:13,865 --> 00:38:16,145
for you all that you never got to finish.

417
00:38:24,585 --> 00:38:27,905
TOMB OF RAN FANGXU

418
00:38:27,985 --> 00:38:29,145
Uncle Ran,

419
00:38:30,025 --> 00:38:31,465
I'm not going to Beijing anymore.

420
00:38:32,425 --> 00:38:35,985
No matter how cold or heavy something is,

421
00:38:36,505 --> 00:38:38,265
I'll carry it myself.

422
00:38:38,345 --> 00:38:40,305
I'll carry it all by myself.

423
00:39:18,145 --> 00:39:21,625
WEIYANG PUBLIC SECURITY BUREAU
NANSHAN BRANCH

424
00:39:23,385 --> 00:39:26,265
<i>Wang Xinglong said</i>
<i>the night before New Year's Eve,</i>

425
00:39:26,345 --> 00:39:28,665
<i>Ran stayed in New York Block</i>
<i>the whole night.</i>

426
00:39:28,745 --> 00:39:32,345
<i>He must've found</i>
<i>some crucial information or a clue.</i>

427
00:39:32,425 --> 00:39:34,425
That's why the next day
he wrote that message.

428
00:39:36,305 --> 00:39:38,625
I'm not leaving this building.

429
00:39:39,225 --> 00:39:41,825
I'll ask Captain Zhao
to reopen the June 30th case.

430
00:39:42,345 --> 00:39:45,145
We'll reopen it, but now isn't the time.

431
00:39:45,225 --> 00:39:46,505
<i>We don't have key evidence.</i>

432
00:39:46,585 --> 00:39:49,705
<i>Especially this crucial person,</i>
<i>Yao Xincheng.</i>

433
00:39:49,785 --> 00:39:51,025
We haven't found him yet.

434
00:39:51,625 --> 00:39:52,665
Luckily,

435
00:39:52,745 --> 00:39:55,825
Ran narrowed the final clue
down to Yuanlongli.

436
00:39:56,465 --> 00:39:58,225
-I'll investigate with you.
-<i>No need.</i>

437
00:39:58,305 --> 00:40:00,265
If we go together, we'll draw attention.

438
00:40:00,345 --> 00:40:02,825
<i>It'll be easier if I work alone.</i>

439
00:40:02,905 --> 00:40:04,265
<i>Get the application papers ready now.</i>

440
00:40:04,345 --> 00:40:06,065
<i>Once I make progress here,</i>

441
00:40:06,145 --> 00:40:09,745
go to Zhao Jie and have him coordinate
a delay to Yuanlongli's demolition.

442
00:40:10,665 --> 00:40:11,545
Also…

443
00:40:13,785 --> 00:40:15,065
Hello? Hello?

444
00:40:15,145 --> 00:40:16,185
Hello?

445
00:40:18,025 --> 00:40:19,065
Lousy signal.

446
00:40:20,105 --> 00:40:21,465
NO SERVICE

447
00:40:23,345 --> 00:40:24,305
Jeez.

448
00:40:25,025 --> 00:40:26,425
No signal again.

449
00:40:42,625 --> 00:40:43,905
Mr. He,

450
00:40:43,985 --> 00:40:45,305
you went back on your word.

451
00:40:45,385 --> 00:40:47,105
You said you would move out
before demolition.

452
00:40:47,185 --> 00:40:48,305
You let down my trust.

453
00:40:49,585 --> 00:40:50,425
Good timing.

454
00:40:50,505 --> 00:40:54,025
Didn't you want me to move out early?
Find a person for me.

455
00:40:54,945 --> 00:40:57,705
Ask around whether anyone
named Yao Xincheng

456
00:40:57,785 --> 00:41:00,665
was living in Yuanlongli around 1997.

457
00:41:00,745 --> 00:41:03,225
Or anyone who knows this person.

458
00:41:03,985 --> 00:41:05,185
-Yao Xincheng?
-Right.

459
00:41:06,665 --> 00:41:09,305
Never heard of any Yao Xincheng.

460
00:41:09,905 --> 00:41:12,105
Mr. He, tell me honestly.

461
00:41:12,185 --> 00:41:13,465
You refuse to leave here

462
00:41:13,545 --> 00:41:15,745
because you want to investigate
the case from 1997 again?

463
00:41:16,665 --> 00:41:18,585
Are you acting up again?

464
00:41:19,505 --> 00:41:20,785
My mind is perfectly fine.

465
00:41:20,865 --> 00:41:22,505
Don't listen to their nonsense.

466
00:41:23,225 --> 00:41:24,825
Seems like you're still not quite right.

467
00:41:26,425 --> 00:41:31,305
Mr. He, Officer Ran and you
solved the Yuanlongli case twice.

468
00:41:31,945 --> 00:41:33,305
You even got a commendation
the second time.

469
00:41:33,385 --> 00:41:36,265
Are you trying to overturn it
and solve it a third time?

470
00:41:36,785 --> 00:41:39,505
Until the truth is found,
forget a third time.

471
00:41:39,585 --> 00:41:40,945
A fourth time. A fifth time.

472
00:41:41,025 --> 00:41:43,185
Even if it takes a hundred times,
I'll keep digging.

473
00:41:44,345 --> 00:41:46,825
This is the task
Ran left me before he died.

474
00:41:46,905 --> 00:41:48,265
If I can't finish it,

475
00:41:48,345 --> 00:41:50,745
I won't have the face
to meet him down there.

476
00:41:54,345 --> 00:41:57,425
This was Officer Ran's last wish?

477
00:41:57,505 --> 00:41:58,625
Right.

478
00:42:05,385 --> 00:42:07,465
For someone as good as Officer Ran,

479
00:42:08,225 --> 00:42:10,545
I'll help with this.

480
00:42:11,145 --> 00:42:15,425
Tell me. Aside from Yao Xincheng,
what else do you need me to do?

481
00:42:17,505 --> 00:42:20,785
Can you restore
the signal, water, and electricity?

482
00:42:20,865 --> 00:42:22,625
-Alright.
-By the way,

483
00:42:22,705 --> 00:42:26,985
if possible, tell Qian Dajun
not to start demolition early.

484
00:42:27,745 --> 00:42:28,825
I'll do everything I can to help.

485
00:42:29,465 --> 00:42:32,225
Qian Dajun is downstairs.
Wait for my news.

486
00:42:32,305 --> 00:42:34,145
Okay?

487
00:42:48,065 --> 00:42:52,825
ROUND 4 OF THE TRÉMAUX ALGORITHM
ON THE YUANLONGLI CASE

488
00:43:09,105 --> 00:43:10,065
HOLDOUTS GROUP

489
00:43:10,145 --> 00:43:11,745
DU: MR. HE, HURRY OVER!

490
00:43:13,065 --> 00:43:14,385
DU

491
00:43:14,465 --> 00:43:16,705
<i>Mr. He, help me! Get to the cybercafé now!</i>

492
00:43:20,105 --> 00:43:22,825
This man…

493
00:43:22,905 --> 00:43:24,465
OPTICAL

494
00:43:24,545 --> 00:43:25,745
Brat,

495
00:43:26,705 --> 00:43:28,185
listen up.

496
00:43:28,745 --> 00:43:30,105
Move aside right now.

497
00:43:30,945 --> 00:43:32,505
My patience is running out.

498
00:43:33,265 --> 00:43:36,145
Don't come over! Don't come over!

499
00:43:36,785 --> 00:43:37,505
I'll count to three.

500
00:43:38,665 --> 00:43:40,185
If you don't move,

501
00:43:40,265 --> 00:43:41,625
I'll tear down this darned building
with you in it.

502
00:43:41,705 --> 00:43:43,105
I'll stand with my shop.

503
00:43:43,185 --> 00:43:45,665
If you dare come closer,
I'll take you down with me!

504
00:43:46,945 --> 00:43:48,145
One.

505
00:43:48,785 --> 00:43:50,065
Two.

506
00:43:51,545 --> 00:43:52,705
-Three.
-Qian Dajun,

507
00:43:53,545 --> 00:43:55,385
what you're doing now counts as a crime.

508
00:43:55,465 --> 00:43:56,625
Get down here.

509
00:43:57,745 --> 00:43:58,905
Crazy old fool.

510
00:43:59,425 --> 00:44:01,105
Still think you're a cop?

511
00:44:03,465 --> 00:44:04,985
HAIR SALON

512
00:44:09,305 --> 00:44:10,585
I'm fighting you today!

513
00:44:10,665 --> 00:44:12,345
Come on then. Don't stop me, Mr. He!

514
00:44:12,425 --> 00:44:13,625
I'll hack him to death!

515
00:44:15,425 --> 00:44:16,785
